{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#1484","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#1484","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#1484\",\"parent_revision\":\"0f33acea91ead890aa7aa6542056bcc73324d63db2e622bfb26963b9066bc68e\",\"root_revision\":\"0f33acea91ead890aa7aa6542056bcc73324d63db2e622bfb26963b9066bc68e\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nTwo list-capability gaps in the Backlog MCP server:\\n\\n1. backlog_list_issues has no offset or limit parameters. On repos with many sub-issues it silently truncates results. Callers cannot page through results or know whether truncation occurred.\\n\\n2. backlog_list has no date-range filter. Agents wanting items created or updated within a time window must fetch all items and filter manually, which is expensive on large backlogs.\\n\\nEvidence: server.py lines 2544\u20132565 (backlog_list_issues, no pagination parameters); backlog_list parameter list (no created_after/updated_after fields).\\n\\nVerbatim user report: \\\"group these into combined tasks that can be done via the /python-tdd process\\\"\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **backlog mcp: backlog_list_issues lacks pagination; backlog_list lacks date-range filter** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Research finding \u2014 mcp-ux-improvements-20260404.md, validated mcp-ux-improvements-validation-20260404.md\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-04-05\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"b7cccb998f8a11922a557d1b3505eb23f4890a0bde65d021e43397fb746d8c85\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABSdrsLg\"}"}